1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,895
This is FermFrame.

2
00:00:01,895 --> 00:00:11,349
It turns a cheap desktop clock into a little screen that shows your fermentation, straight from Brewfather or a RAPT Pill.

3
00:00:11,349 --> 00:00:13,596
Let's take a look at the app.

4
00:00:15,467 --> 00:00:19,660
Download FermFrame from its GitHub page and open it.

5
00:00:19,660 --> 00:00:20,789
Click Install.

6
00:00:20,789 --> 00:00:27,402
It installs just for you, with no admin rights, and adds itself to the Start menu.

7
00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:30,590
This is the main window.

8
00:00:30,590 --> 00:00:32,844
On the left are your FermFrames.

9
00:00:32,844 --> 00:00:37,491
A green dot means it's working, and grey means it isn't answering.

10
00:00:39,233 --> 00:00:48,939
For the one you've selected, you see the brew, its gravity, the temperature, the alcohol so far, and how many days it's been fermenting.

11
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:54,384
Underneath is the whole fermentation as a graph.

12
00:00:54,384 --> 00:00:57,380
Gravity in amber, temperature in blue.

13
00:00:58,867 --> 00:01:01,435
Click another FermFrame to see its brew.

14
00:01:01,435 --> 00:01:07,087
When the gravity hasn't moved for three days, it lets you know it might be ready to keg.

15
00:01:08,700 --> 00:01:11,301
Give each one a name that makes sense to you.

16
00:01:15,967 --> 00:01:19,713
The Settings tab changes everything about the screen.

17
00:01:19,713 --> 00:01:25,580
Pick a theme or your own colours, a font, the brightness, and when to dim at night.

18
00:01:30,933 --> 00:01:36,814
Choose the graph style and time range, and which pages it takes turns showing.

19
00:01:36,814 --> 00:01:43,147
The graph, a big number you can read across the room, the time, or your other brews.

20
00:01:44,867 --> 00:01:47,547
Nothing changes until you press Save.

21
00:01:47,547 --> 00:01:50,300
Then the screen updates straight away.

22
00:01:52,100 --> 00:01:55,317
The Firmware tab keeps everything up to date.

23
00:01:55,317 --> 00:01:59,391
One click, about a minute, and it keeps all its settings.

24
00:02:12,233 --> 00:02:13,302
Want another one?

25
00:02:13,302 --> 00:02:17,388
This shows exactly which clock to buy, and which ones won't work.

26
00:02:20,500 --> 00:02:26,389
When it arrives, plug it into power and click Set up a new FermFrame.

27
00:02:26,389 --> 00:02:32,193
Check your Wi-Fi, add your Brewfather details, and press the button.

28
00:02:32,193 --> 00:02:36,290
A few minutes later, your brew is on the screen.

29
00:02:38,033 --> 00:02:39,482
That's FermFrame.

30
00:02:39,482 --> 00:02:44,596
It's free and open source, and the full manual is on GitHub.

31
00:02:44,596 --> 00:02:45,789
Happy brewing.

